A||||5||Majik||I love GM (sort of long text)||||12||
Z||000000||Majik||06-28-2000||09:01 PM||||Well, I just bought my 86 GT in January, and it's had a new clutch, plugs, wires, and rotors put on it in the first two weeks...but I was dreading the manifold leak on the rear of the engine (which is why it sat in the driveway with the occasional drive).  I priced it out and it was out of my price range, as well as knowing good and well that those bolts (from the condition of the pipe) were all rusted.<P>Long story short, I took it to my local Pontiac dealer in the short shot that the recall on the engine fires hadn't been done (which only covers the front exaust manifold (according to the recall paperwork)).  They took the recall and told me they'd put a bead of weld around the crack for me and that would last me a few months until I could fix it.<P>They called me the next day and told me that both manifolds were going to be replaced due to warranty coverage (probally meaning that somewhere that I didn't read said that in case of crack, replace other manifold).  Anyways, the car passed emissions today first time through on a car that hadn't been taken very well care of!  Its legal, and I'm finally driving my new fiero!  Pics will come sometime in the future...but wanted to brag just a bit to you all!  On cloud 9 today!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>By the way, the dealership said that the recall kit for the engine fire, was the last one that gm had in inventory...if this is indeed true...my luck is improving!<P>Glad to be driving a Fiero again!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>_-_Majik_-_||||reg||12
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||06-29-2000||12:31 AM||||Sounds like it was your lucky day !!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||06-29-2000||02:07 AM||||How long did it take them to do the work?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Coconut||06-29-2000||03:01 AM||||Just goes to show ya........ Good things come to those ......who drive Fieros! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||06-29-2000||09:50 AM||||Majik. Congrats! Always good to hear something work out like that.<BR>However... GM didn't just do this out of the goodness of their hearts. They are pretty much required by law to perform the recall work, if it hasn't been done. If they didn't have the parts, I suspect they would have had to find them somewhere. (Someone please correct me if I'm wrong.)<BR>But I'm <I>not</I> cynical.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Majik||06-29-2000||02:17 PM||||It took them 3 days to get the parts in, I turned my car in on Thursday, then they had to order the other manifold.  They had the manifold in and car done by Monday afternoon.  They told me that the work could be done in one day...I'm sure that depends on the amount of work they have going.<P>Majik||||reg||1
